{"title":"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> be a triangle. A circle passing through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> intersects segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. Lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/5/6d5c9afa92ae3180f02754c177e530d9d0f8b4d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, while lines <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/d/07d29465728e92952374a857beaee91665d8dbd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CF$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Prove that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b4fb15e1f7f5e609ad8e174a11d73764443dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF = MC$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec668df521576b61f9d226ede4a4196329f73fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB\\cdot MD = MC^2$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Extend segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/5/1f5d96c8d1e481244e028c9e97d1d7b53206536b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$DM$\" width=\"34\" height=\"12\" /> through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/2/6e28ce12d49d39f160d5a0ef54077fc98e4b9d2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/c/f7c1cf9a6838ac5a482645bf581efb0b2e21b5b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FG\\parallel CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aebb0446ff1f10ad418ae2cce5809fb8a1cd38d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(10)+0.6); size(250); var theta=22, r=0.58; pair B=origin, A=dir(theta), C=A+(rotate(78)*0.8*A), O=IP(CR(B,r),CR(A,r)); path c=CR(O,r); pair D=IP(c,A--C), E=IP(c,B--C), F=extension(A,B,D,E), M=extension(B,D,C,F), G=extension(D,M,F,F+C-D); draw(A--B--C--A^^E--F--C^^A--F^^B--M^^E--M); draw(c); draw(F--G--C^^M--G,gray+0.4); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(F-E)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,2*dir(B-A)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*dir(C-A)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,2.5*dir(250)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,2.5*dir(C-A)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,dir(F-E)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,2.5*dir(255)); dot(&quot;$G$&quot;,G,dir(G-M)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"398\" />\nThen <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b4fb15e1f7f5e609ad8e174a11d73764443dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF = MC$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac587b949b37145c39345a654a1952c9d7615740.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDFG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a parallelogram, or, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/c/27cd15d74a73d20543577ebd9b4019a87a7fbccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FD\\parallel CG$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"77\" height=\"19\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3103f15d54db7b08ff86e4d5e255a4dabfe8816c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = MF$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/9/4f9cdb99124146c4eb61af37ed0d3763efb89aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle GCD = \\angle FDA$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />, that is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/f/a0fdce0a486ee5f5a1bef9c72893185528e96eec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FDA + \\angle CGF = 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"195\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p><p>Because quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68eca3ba7f3e3a5f5b07a373f664d66e17f9d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/2/0a2a58dc4a6f61820e497917d098924669f592b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FDA = \\angle ABE$\" width=\"135\" height=\"13\" />. It follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3103f15d54db7b08ff86e4d5e255a4dabfe8816c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = MF$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/0395eabfc7c89d016cf2151837291dafb5c6157e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[180^\\circ = \\angle FDA + \\angle CGF = \\angle ABE + \\angle CGF,\\]\" width=\"351\" height=\"16\" />\nthat is, quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/c/b3c766151f7dcfb812e2403ebb0f7b74788bd975.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CBFG$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" /> is cyclic, which is equivalent to\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec46ab45c1061beecee50e19e3131ebf749a82d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle CBM = \\angle CBG = \\angle CFG = \\angle DCF = \\angle DCM.\\]\" width=\"391\" height=\"12\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd866b6157f91729bf61f4b9c6c7dbf5c1ee85e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DMC = \\angle CMB$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4dcd899a14318cd768c2ac025ab0591fb9b1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBM = \\angle DCM$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/9/dc99161e3a8296e77b2fb2b5a44f0eb0d0711d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCM$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ef54a96b558f4dc28307ddc3e86cb48d81a978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDM$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> are similar, that is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/3/593e30095f2345f432594b1500cb8abf3cd7966f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{CM}{BM} = \\frac{DM}{CM},\\]\" width=\"104\" height=\"37\" />\nor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec668df521576b61f9d226ede4a4196329f73fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB\\cdot MD = MC^2$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We first assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec668df521576b61f9d226ede4a4196329f73fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB\\cdot MD = MC^2$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />. Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/a/57abff498db22aba43d6158b456f20ec592a2a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{MC}{MD} = \\frac{MB}{MC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/6/3560e6284d8df050fa75c3f296d53c3b55ba3623.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMD = \\angle BMC$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" />, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3f7db9e5618aa83bb58ddccac7693cf92a75d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CMD$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/1/5b1a0f691e308462e4fe9b0476508ef0b065423c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BMC$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> are similar. Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47e1b9aab80dea9a5e62bdfd28556211774bc7d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle MCD = \\angle MBC$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" />. This exact condition can also be visualized through power of M with respect to the circumcircle of triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/5/4057c3e63298c2ed6715003afb6f2d9dc6272037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BDC$\" width=\"44\" height=\"12\" /> and getting the angle condition from the alternate segment theorem.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/c/dccc58236ee7334fa70404b585f3c4c981d11ac7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(10)+0.6); size(250); var theta=22, r=0.58; pair B=origin, A=dir(theta), C=A+(rotate(78)*0.8*A), O=IP(CR(B,r),CR(A,r)); path c=CR(O,r); pair D=IP(c,A--C), E=IP(c,B--C), F=extension(A,B,D,E), M=extension(B,D,C,F), G=extension(D,M,F,F+C-D); draw(A--B--C--A^^E--F--C^^A--F^^B--M^^E--M); draw(c); draw(A--E,gray+0.4); dot(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,dir(F-E)); dot(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,2*dir(B-A)); dot(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,1.5*dir(C-A)); dot(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,2.5*dir(250)); dot(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,2.5*dir(C-A)); dot(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,dir(F-E)); dot(&quot;$M$&quot;,M,2.5*dir(255)); [/asy]\" width=\"418\" height=\"398\" />\nBecause quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68eca3ba7f3e3a5f5b07a373f664d66e17f9d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd239ea6779d98dc4fa0dd7ece79411235cb39a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAE = \\angle DBE$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />. Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/c/08c5465deb3369ba481824d3f53228b62332ac28.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle FCA = \\angle MCD = \\angle MBC = \\angle DBE = \\angle DAE = \\angle CAE,\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"16\" />\nimplying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b631ddfe96ce2567b9390220182dac992fc5e321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE\\parallel CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a608aaa4a0526582db306730a79cc087bae2518.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AEF = \\angle CFE$\" width=\"134\" height=\"13\" />. Because quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68eca3ba7f3e3a5f5b07a373f664d66e17f9d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8227ca174e83b9a43b8eb2fc59bc0338db881e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD = \\angle AED$\" width=\"137\" height=\"13\" />. Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/c/c2c6a78b1538c354f9d4128c5ef0ea74e0cdef1c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle FBM = \\angle ABD = \\angle AED = \\angle AEF = \\angle CFE = \\angle MFD.\\]\" width=\"472\" height=\"13\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/9/d390f6382a56e08cdfa416816b81ceb6df765797.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FBM = \\angle DFM$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/8/2d8871186a86ae2c84531f3b10b9f3559346a9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle FMB = \\angle DMF$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" />, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/5/f351183ba082de9b0f8cdf8a9e72faa0bd2bc4a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BFM$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/d/a1d50b559097e36a71b4afbcecac3b6d21232e25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FDM$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" /> are similar. Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/2/5d2188027aa7b2b0e54cadb962583c313ecc9e63.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{FM}{DM} = \\frac{BM}{FM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3ee84547e21b069265f35a7495bd408cb7b3a73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$FM^2 = BM\\cdot DM = CM^2$\" width=\"212\" height=\"15\" />. Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23da5b3e765ca7d70f9abc6bedc8d7418fd4715d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC^2 = MB\\cdot MD$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" /> implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3103f15d54db7b08ff86e4d5e255a4dabfe8816c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = MF$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Now we assume that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3103f15d54db7b08ff86e4d5e255a4dabfe8816c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MC = MF$\" width=\"92\" height=\"12\" />. Applying Ceva's Theorem to triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a3f0e3dd12e6a4cc523abc05db1a2bce99298d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCF$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and cevians <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/0/87044040051898eada63f29492ccde6da8ac5a23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM, CA, FE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"105\" height=\"16\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/0/1/9013b57cfcff737dcbf16ba73771632f31c1ae11.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{BA}{AF}\\cdot\\frac{FM}{MC}\\cdot\\frac{CE}{EB} = 1,\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"37\" />\nimplying that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6f742257fa694737edd1e389e8484fb34d08c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{BA}{AF} = \\frac{BE}{EC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"88\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/3/b631ddfe96ce2567b9390220182dac992fc5e321.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE\\parallel CF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"19\" />.\n</p><p>Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41d37d35cdaf597aaae6c7e39b52d50aa7c2d90d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DCM = \\angle DAE$\" width=\"142\" height=\"13\" />. Because quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/8/a68eca3ba7f3e3a5f5b07a373f664d66e17f9d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is cyclic, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/2/cd239ea6779d98dc4fa0dd7ece79411235cb39a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle DAE = \\angle DBE$\" width=\"138\" height=\"13\" />. Hence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a3b61c914a74f7db09b7a82b125913019c269b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle DCM = \\angle DAE = \\angle DBE = \\angle CBM.\\]\" width=\"312\" height=\"13\" />\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/4/ea4dcd899a14318cd768c2ac025ab0591fb9b1af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CBM = \\angle DCM$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/a/93a34d21ff3f180e82bcfbe8e578e4e833eb9804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CMB = \\angle DMC$\" width=\"147\" height=\"12\" />, triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/9/dc99161e3a8296e77b2fb2b5a44f0eb0d0711d6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BCM$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/e/15ef54a96b558f4dc28307ddc3e86cb48d81a978.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CDM$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" /> are similar. Consequently, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/d/9cd3a4db764008accdfc11e4e8968ba07350c5d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{CM}{DM} = \\frac{BM}{CM}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/3/4731b824fca8aac12e1c3c7a4eb6f4ad3133371a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CM^2 = BM\\cdot DM$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>Combining the above, we conclude that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/b/07b4fb15e1f7f5e609ad8e174a11d73764443dc4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MF = MC$\" width=\"91\" height=\"12\" /> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/c/bec668df521576b61f9d226ede4a4196329f73fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MB\\cdot MD = MC^2$\" width=\"147\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p><i>Alternate solutions are always welcome. If you have a different, elegant solution to this problem, please <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit\">add it</a> to this page.</i>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO\" title=\"2003 USAMO\">2003 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2003\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2003 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017202647\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.055 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.080 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 456/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1663/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 48/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 14763/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   19.880      1 -total\n 40.36%    8.023      1 Template:USAMO_newbox\n 30.70%    6.103      1 Template:Alternate_solutions\n 26.83%    5.334      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7174:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017202647 and revision id 186204. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}